Ladybird’s storage.<area>.getKeys() lists the area’s keys in insertion
order and takes no arguments. Chromium exposes it on every area through
StorageStorageAreaGetKeysFunction (extensions/browser/api/storage/
storage_api.cc), which asks StorageFrontend::GetKeys() for the keys
alone. Gecko’s ext-storage.js routes storage.local to
ExtensionStorage.getKeys() (or ExtensionStorageIDB’s getKeys()) and
storage.session to extensionStorageSession.getKeys(), which returns the
bucket’s keys. WebKit declares getKeys() in
WebExtensionAPIStorageArea.idl and reads the keys from its SQLite store.
